      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "Determine the prevalence and risk factors of wheeze and severe wheeze in 13-to 14-year-old children."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "The study was conducted August 2004 to February 2005 in the Polokwane area, South Africa."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The 12-month prevalence rate was 18.9% for wheeze and 9.2% for severe wheeze (n = 3,926). The presence of other allergic symptoms and industrial activities appear to increase the likelihood of wheeze, even more so for severe wheeze. Socioeconomic-related factors appear to have a protective effect on wheeze."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Wheeze appears to be a substantial public health problem in the Polokwane area."
        }
      ]},
